### EasyTier (optional LAN/tunnel sidecar)

- Project: EasyTier — https://github.com/EasyTier/EasyTier
- Version used by the design: **2.7.0** (fixed version; SHA-256 is verified)
- License: **LGPL-3.0**
- How it is used: as a **separate executable process** (`easytier-core`),
  downloaded at runtime from the official release after user consent. It is
  **not** linked into this application, **not** modified, and **not** bundled
  by default. Users may replace it with their own build/path.
- LGPL-3.0 text and source location are provided alongside the component
  (`dataRoot/modules/link/licenses/EasyTier-LICENSE.txt` when installed), and
  the project source is available at the URL above (version tag `v2.7.0`).
- The application's own GPL-3.0 license and EasyTier's LGPL-3.0 are compatible;
  see `docs/02-compliance-security.md` §6.6.

### authlib-injector (optional third-party account support)

- Project: authlib-injector — https://github.com/yushijinhun/authlib-injector
- Version used in acceptance: **1.2.8** (fixed version; SHA-256 verified)
- License: **AGPL-3.0 with an explicit exception** that permits unmodified
  binary distribution and Java Agent loading.
- How it is used: downloaded at runtime from the official release and loaded as
  an unmodified `-javaagent` for third-party (Authlib/Yggdrasil) accounts. The
  project does not modify its code. Its license text is shipped/displayed with
  the component as required.

### Minecraft / Mojang

- Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB / Microsoft.
- This is an **unofficial** launcher and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
  sponsored by Mojang or Microsoft.
- The launcher **does not distribute Minecraft game files or Mojang assets**.
  Version metadata and files are downloaded by the launcher at the user's
  request from Mojang endpoints or configured mirrors. Users are responsible for
  owning a legitimate Minecraft account where required.
- Offline accounts are for single-player/LAN use; the launcher does not provide
  or endorse bypassing Mojang authentication or joining online servers without
  a valid account.

### Modrinth

- Project/data source: https://modrinth.com / https://api.modrinth.com
- Mod metadata and files belong to their respective authors and Modrinth.
- The launcher uses a single identifying User-Agent, respects the documented
  rate limit (≤300 requests/minute), downloads directly from `cdn.modrinth.com`,
  verifies `sha1`/`sha512`, does not re-host or mirror Modrinth files, and does
  not bundle them in the installer.
- Modrinth API usage is subject to Modrinth's terms; see
  `docs/02-compliance-security.md` §5.1.

### CurseForge

- P0 **does not call the CurseForge API** and contains **no CurseForge API key**.
  It only opens project pages in the browser and parses local pack zips.
- P1 may integrate CurseForge only with the operator's own official API key and
  after the legal prerequisites in `docs/02-compliance-security.md` §5.2
  (key not exposed in client, no API-data caching, no proxy anonymity,
  competitor-terms review) are satisfied.

### BMCLAPI / mirrors

- BMCLAPI is a third-party mirror service; mirrored files remain the property of
  their source sites. It is not an open-source service and provides no SLA.
- The launcher displays the active download source in the UI and logs it; the
  mirror can be disabled. The launcher does not re-package BMCLAPI as its own
  public API/mirror.

### Plain Craft Launcher 2 (PCL2)

- This project is an independent clean-room implementation. It does **not**
  include, copy, port, or redistribute PCL2 source code, icons, backgrounds,
  music, skin assets, or other bundled resources.
- PCL2 is not open source; its distribution is governed by the author's
  "PCL 分发有限许可". See `docs/clean-room-log.md` and
  `docs/02-compliance-security.md` for the clean-room record.

### Other services

- Microsoft/Xbox Live authentication endpoints are used only for the user's own
  Microsoft account, with the user's consent; tokens are stored encrypted with
  Electron `safeStorage` (DPAPI on Windows) where persistence is implemented.
- No telemetry is sent by this project.

